<title>USA: Integrated Circuit sells Galaxy to ex-CEO.</title>
<headline>Integrated Circuit sells Galaxy to ex-CEO.</headline>
<dateline>VALLEY FORGE, Pa. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integrated Circuit Systems Inc said Thursday it has sold its battery charge controller business to Edward Arnold, a director and former chairman and chief executive officer of the company.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the sale, Arnold acquired the company's Galaxy Power Inc unit in exchange for shares of the company's stock held by Arnold.</p>
<p>A company spokesman was not immediately available to say how many shares were involved in the transaction.</p>
</text>
